# Cline pointer → web-research skill

This project includes a skill named **web-research** at `.cline/skills/web-research/SKILL.md`.

When you need to **search the web, read page content, or verify information** — e.g. the user gives
content to verify, asks about the latest version/news/price, provides a URL to read, hits an error
to look up, or mentions a technology/term that should be checked against up-to-date sources — **read
`.cline/skills/web-research/SKILL.md` and follow it** — it now contains the search-strategy guidance
(query design, search operators, verification) inline, so there is nothing else to open.

Principle: **do not search blindly.** Decompose the request → decide whether a search is actually
needed → one goal per query, using precise terms → read the original source, not just the snippet →
cross-check when it matters → answer with the URL and a TRUE/FALSE/OUTDATED verdict.
